<title>USA: PennFed Financial discontinues buyback plan.</title>
<headline>PennFed Financial discontinues buyback plan.</headline>
<dateline>WEST ORANGE, N.J. 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>PennFed Financial Services Inc said it discontinued its five percent stock buyback plan, previously approved September 16.</p>
<p>The company did not say why it discontinued the plan. Officials there were not immediately available to comment.</p>
<p>Under the plan, the company has so far bought back 32,500 shares -- or 0.7 percent of its total outstanding shares -- at an average price of $20.04, it said.</p>
<p>The company said it will use the capital it would have spent on the shares to fund growth in its retail operations.</p>
